    {
      "code": "CSCI26_CE3",
      "title": "Gate chain with XOR, NOR, NAND",
      "type": "multi",
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "md": "Three inputs A, B, C feed a chain of gates. $G_1 = A \\oplus B$ (XOR). $G_2$ is NOR of $G_1$ and C. OUT is NAND of $G_2$ and A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "md": "Evaluate the chain in that order for each row: $(A, B, C) = (1, 0, 1)$, then $(0, 1, 0)$, then $(1, 1, 0)$. Work one gate at a time, and write down $G_1$ and $G_2$ for every row before you read OUT."
        }
      ],
      "how": "Type 0 or 1 for OUT in each row, in the order given.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "type": "text",
          "answer": "1",
          "accept": [
            "1"
          ],
          "wrong": [
            {
              "match": "0",
              "error": "negation",
              "hint": "QUACK. NAND is NOT of AND. What is $G_2$ here, and what does A add?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "type": "text",
          "answer": "1",
          "accept": [
            "1"
          ],
          "wrong": [
            {
              "match": "0",
              "error": "negation",
              "hint": "QUACK. NOR is true only when both inputs are 0. Recheck $G_2$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "type": "text",
          "answer": "0",
          "accept": [
            "0"
          ],
          "wrong": [
            {
              "match": "1",
              "error": "negation",
              "hint": "QUACK. XOR of equal inputs is 0. What does NOR do with 0 and 0?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "nudge": "QUACK. One gate at a time: $G_1$ first, then $G_2$, then OUT."
    },
